From fff878ecdeda7205d59e69fb420d9f2f0d6ccbd2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kernel-experiments <kernel-experiments@localhost>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:36:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 12/17] inkling2/cuda: pair same-input Q8_0 projections into
 one mmvq launch; stage aliased inputs of fused runs

- graph: Q + gate (and K + V when they share the input) are expanded next to each other; values unchanged,
  the allocator plans the new order (verified bit-exact with the pair fusion off).
- mmvq pair mode: the second matrix runs in the shared_up grid slice of the same kernel (same per-row
  arithmetic). Fixes has_fusion ignoring shared_up, which made the extra slice recompute matrix A out of bounds.
- QKV_POST / RELBIAS_T: inputs that the allocator planned under an output are copied to scratch by a tiny
  stage kernel instead of rejecting the fusion (the reorder had made 20 RELBIAS_T and some QKV_POST fall back).
Decode bit-identical. Interleaved screen: tg128 0K 62.44/62.74/62.08, 8K 56.06/56.40/55.83.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
